UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Horizontal price-fixing among competing sellers","Price discrimination in selling commodities of like grade and quality","Tying arrangements that condition one product on purchasing another","Monopolization through exclusive dealing contracts"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): The Robinson-Patman Act (1936) amends the Clayton Act and specifically prohibits price discrimination in the sale of commodities of like grade and quality where the effect may substantially lessen competition. It targets sellers offering unjustifiably different prices to competing buyers purchasing similar quantities.
Wrong (A): Horizontal price-fixing is a per se violation under Section 1 of the Sherman Act, not the Robinson-Patman Act.
Wrong (C): Tying arrangements are addressed under Section 3 of the Clayton Act, not the Robinson-Patman Act.
Wrong (D): Exclusive dealing contracts are governed by Section 3 of the Clayton Act and Section 5 of the FTC Act, not the Robinson-Patman Act.$EXPL$
