-- Q11296: Government Regulation of Business [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A tying arrangement conditioning one product sale on buying another","Price discrimination by offering unmatched bundled pricing to buyers","A group boycott effectively excluding competing storage vendors","Predatory pricing by selling storage below cost to eliminate rivals"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 3 of the Clayton Act, a tying arrangement occurs when a seller conditions the sale of one product (the tying product) on the buyer''s purchase of a separate product (the tied product). Dominion''s requirement that customers buy its storage service with the accounting platform is a classic tie.
Wrong (B): Price discrimination under the Robinson-Patman Act involves charging different buyers different prices for the same product, not conditioning purchases on buying a second product.
Wrong (C): A group boycott involves competitors collectively refusing to deal with a party, which is not the scenario here.
Wrong (D): Predatory pricing requires selling below cost with intent to eliminate competition, which is not alleged in this fact pattern.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11296;

