-- Q74: Like-Kind Exchanges [easy/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Section 1031 allows tax-deferred exchanges of real property held for productive use in a trade or business or for investment. Ramirez''s warehouse-for-shopping-center exchange qualifies because both are real property. Cho''s stock exchange fails because Section 1031(a)(2) explicitly excludes stocks, bonds, and securities, even if the underlying companies own real estate.
Wrong (A): While the analysis of Ramirez is correct, this choice also correctly states Cho does not qualify — making it the right answer rather than a wrong one.
Wrong (B): Securities representing indirect ownership of real property do not satisfy Section 1031. The taxpayer must exchange real property directly.
Wrong (D): Different types of real estate (warehouse vs. shopping center) are considered like-kind under Section 1031. The like-kind standard for real estate is broad.$EXPL$
