-- Q75: Like-Kind Exchanges [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): In a Section 1031 exchange, gain is recognized to the extent of boot (cash or non-like-kind property) received, but never exceeds the realized gain. Callahan''s realized gain is $150,000 ($350,000 FMV minus $200,000 basis), but recognition is limited to the $50,000 boot received. Drake receives no boot, so no gain is recognized.
Wrong (B): This choice incorrectly states both recognize $0. Callahan must recognize gain equal to the $50,000 boot received because that portion was not reinvested in like-kind property.
Wrong (C): Boot does not trigger full gain recognition. Under Section 1031(b), gain is recognized only to the extent of boot received, not the entire realized gain.
Wrong (D): Pure exchanges without boot receive the most favorable treatment ($0 recognition), not harsher treatment. This reverses the actual rule.$EXPL$
