-- Q89: Partnerships [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 732(a)(2), in a nonliquidating distribution, property basis cannot exceed the partner''s remaining outside basis. Cash reduces outside basis first under Section 733. Xavier''s $60,000 basis minus $45,000 cash leaves $15,000, so the property takes a $15,000 basis (not its $25,000 inside basis). Yates receives no cash, so the property retains its $25,000 carryover basis.
Wrong (A): Property does not always retain its inside basis. When a cash distribution first reduces outside basis, the remaining basis may be insufficient to support the full carryover.
