-- Q204: Business Law: Contracts [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 14, a minor lacks full contractual capacity, making contracts voidable at the minor''s option. Ethan may disaffirm the contract during minority or within a reasonable time after reaching the age of majority.
Wrong (A): The contract is not void. A void contract has no legal effect from inception. Contracts with minors are voidable, meaning they are enforceable unless the minor elects to disaffirm.
Wrong (C): The contract is not fully enforceable against the minor. The minor''s lack of capacity provides the right to avoid the agreement, which is the core protection for minors.
Wrong (D): Only the minor has the power to disaffirm. The adult party (Valley Motors) is bound by the contract and cannot unilaterally avoid it.$EXPL$
