-- Q205: Agency and Regulation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 4.01, a principal may ratify an unauthorized act by the agent, binding the principal as though the agent had actual authority. Ratification requires the principal to have full knowledge of material facts and to accept the entire transaction.
Wrong (A): The agent''s subjective belief about having authority does not create actual or apparent authority. Authority must derive from the principal''s manifestations, not the agent''s assumptions.
Wrong (C): The third party''s awareness of the agency relationship relates to disclosed vs. undisclosed principal analysis, not to whether the principal can be bound by ratification.
Wrong (D): Good intentions do not create authority or bind the principal. Agency law focuses on the principal''s manifestations and consent, not the agent''s motives.$EXPL$
