  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency, agents owe fiduciary duties of loyalty (Section 8.01), obedience, care, accounting, and notification. However, agents have no duty to independently set the principal''s strategic direction — that responsibility belongs to the principal, not the agent.
Wrong (A): The duty of loyalty is a genuine fiduciary duty requiring the agent to act solely in the principal''s interest and avoid conflicts of interest under Section 8.01.
Wrong (B): The duty of obedience is a genuine fiduciary duty requiring the agent to follow the principal''s lawful instructions and directions.
Wrong (D): The duty of care is a genuine fiduciary duty requiring the agent to act with the competence expected of a reasonable professional in performing assigned tasks.$EXPL$
