-- Q213: Property Transactions: Basis [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treasury Regulation Section 1.168(i)-4(b), when a personal residence is converted to rental property, the depreciation basis is the lower of adjusted basis or FMV at conversion. Foster''s basis is $260,000 (FMV) because the $40,000 decline occurred during personal use, when losses are nondeductible under IRC Section 165(c). Allowing depreciation on full cost would let the taxpayer recover a personal loss through business deductions.
Wrong (A): The lower-of-cost-or-FMV rule does not create an immediately recognizable loss. It simply limits the depreciable basis to prevent deducting personal-use declines.
Wrong (C): The taxpayer cannot elect to use original cost when FMV is lower at conversion. The lower-of-cost-or-FMV rule is mandatory, not elective.
Wrong (D): The rule uses FMV only when it is lower than cost. If FMV exceeded cost, the original cost would serve as the depreciation basis, not FMV.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 213;

